{"availability":"available","full":"KegangWangCCNU/FacePhys-Demo","name":"FacePhys-Demo","description":"FacePhys Web Demo","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"JavaScript","stars":64,"forks":14,"created":"2025-12-22T23:59:37Z","updated":"2026-08-03T07:31:06Z","license":null,"branch":"main","homepage":"https://kegangwangccnu.github.io/FacePhys-Demo/","topics":["ai","biometrics","computer-vision","demo","live","opensource-apps","physiology","real-time","rppg"],"demo":"https://kegangwangccnu.github.io/FacePhys-Demo/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-17T14:29:39.021Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-17T14:29:39.021Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-17T14:29:39.021Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T11:08:17.213Z","stars":64,"forks":14},{"at":"2026-10-10T21:01:07.941Z","stars":64,"forks":14},{"at":"2026-10-11T11:07:09.393Z","stars":64,"forks":14},{"at":"2026-10-17T14:29:39.021Z","stars":64,"forks":14}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Live Demo: Note: A proxy might be required in restricted network regions.","FacePhys Demo is a browser-based remote photoplethysmography (rPPG) monitor. It uses State Space Models (SSMs) to extract heart rate and heart rate variability from facial video feeds via a standard webcam.","The application runs inference locally using LiteRT and WebAssembly. It is designed for edge environments, offering low latency (5ms) with a model size of approximately 4MB."],"features":["State Space Models: Models heart dynamics as continuous-time controlled ODEs to handle irregular sampling.","Multi-threaded Architecture: Uses Web Workers for inference, PSD calculation, and plotting to maintain UI responsiveness.","Visualization: Displays real-time attention heatmaps, 3D state trajectories, and BVP/PSD waveforms.","Interface: Windows 95/98 style UI."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/KegangWangCCNU/FacePhys-Demo/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"0a4c2ca7d010d18f85a1b860c84e675efb3630991fcf3c65160fb